ROOT CAUSE (on-call expert verdict):
  Defect 1: smoke_invoke_bounded() signals only the immediate child
            (kill(pid, ...)). The fake-tart's `sh -c 'sleep 60'` has a
            `sleep` grandchild in the same pgrp. The pgrp signal was
            not used. Orphaned sleep inherits the pipe FDs and holds
            them open.
  Defect 2: handle_tart_guest_smoke() runs sw_vers (30s timeout) THEN
            uname_a (30s timeout) sequentially. The test's 35s socket
            deadline cannot accommodate 60s of helper wallclock, so
            bun's 30s test harness timeout fires first.

EXIT REASON: GS-08 timed out at 30s (bun test harness) before the
            helper could respond (handler was blocked in the post-kill
            pipe drain waiting for the orphan sleep to release the
            pipe FDs).
